# gate/std-fixtures.manifest — the ONLY escape from the std ratchet.
#
# lib/std.id is a tombstone: "NO std namespace. NO std table. NO `std.*`
# spellings in Idol source." GAP-157 is P0 OPEN and says "not as a migration
# alias". Every `std.` spelling in tracked .id source is therefore debt, and
# gate/admission.sh counts it.
#
# A file listed here is a NEGATIVE / COMPATIBILITY FIXTURE: it carries `std.`
# text on purpose, as a detector literal or a diagnostic message, because its
# job is to REJECT that spelling. It is not classified by a regex guess about
# its path or contents; it is classified because a human wrote it down here.
#
# FORMAT — one entry per line:
#     <path><TAB or spaces><exact-count>   # reason
#
# The count is EXACT, not a ceiling. If a fixture gains a literal the gate
# fails; if it loses one the gate also fails. Either way a human re-pins the
# number and states why in the commit. There is no "close enough".
#
# Adding a path here is the whole audit trail. Do not add a path to make a
# failure go away.

gate/idiom.id         18   # idiom scanner: std.script/std.io/std.os detector rows + their self-controls
gate/probe.id         12   # probe scanner: same detector rows, pre-`not`-keyword dialect
gate/host.id           5   # host law: law.world.dot diagnostics naming std.io / std.os, + audit controls
gate/admission.id      2   # admission control A: convicts `std.script.capture` as a fixture input
gate/architecture.id   1   # shell-level control string embedding a literal std.script.capture( pattern
gate/path.id           1   # rule NAME `law.std.zero` in a diagnostic; not a std namespace reach
